cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DRIFT or this repository, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "DRIFT: Decomposing Reasoning Into Failure Types"
abstract: >-
  A solver-instrumented benchmark for evaluating multi-turn constraint
  reasoning in large language models. 1,020 Z3-validated problems across three
  domains (seating, scheduling, logic grids), four solving methods (Direct,
  CoT, Ledger, MUS-Repair), and a decomposition of residual errors into
  satisfiable drift versus contradiction.
